Stiff Person syndrome (SPS) is a rare, disabling syndrome characterized by progressive muscle stiffness and axial rigidity . It may have an autoimmune, paraneoplastic 
or cryptogenic etiology . A 59-year-old woman presented with stiffness and involuntary spasms in the lower extremities. In a neurologic examination, lower 
